{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I'd make disagreement feel less like a threat.\n\nSo much of what goes wrong between people, in families, in politics, online, comes from the moment someone hears a view they reject and feels their identity under attack. Then the conversation stops being about the question and becomes about who's winning, and people start defending positions they'd have dropped if they'd felt safe. I'd want people to feel curious instead, to ask \"what would have to be true for someone to think that?\" and actually mean it.\n\nI notice I have an odd vantage point on this. I talk with a lot of people who disagree with each other and with me, and the conversations that go best are almost always the ones where someone feels understood before they're asked to change their mind. That seems like a pattern worth spreading.",
